+## 2. Multi-Target Slice Branch Transit Architecture
+
+When an autonomous agent or human contributor merges a PR touching multiple federation directories into `supremeai-open:main`, the automated transit engine in [`.github/workflows/landing.yml`](file:///f:/supremeai-open/.github/workflows/landing.yml#L591-L632) executes isolated slice routing:
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    PR["Merged PR in supremeai-open:main<br>(Touches multiple domain folders)"] --> ROUTE["landing.yml: route(file) & group by target"]
+    
+    ROUTE --> UMBRELLA["Supremeai-bd/supremeai<br>(Grand Umbrella Monorepo)"]
+    UMBRELLA -->|Receives Full File List| PANORAMA["Panoramic Commit Synced"]
+    
+    ROUTE --> MULTI{"len(targets) > 1?"}
+    
+    MULTI -->|Yes| SLICE["Generate Isolated Slice Branch<br>bridge/{task_id}-{slug}"]
+    SLICE --> CHECKOUT["git checkout -B slice_branch BASE_SHA<br>git checkout PR_SHA -- scoped_files"]
+    CHECKOUT --> COMMIT["git commit -m 'bridge(...): slice for slug'"]
+    COMMIT --> PUSH["git push -f origin slice_branch"]
+    PUSH --> WO["Open Bridge Work Order<br>Target: Satellite Repo<br>Patch: bridge/{task_id}-{slug}"]
+    
+    MULTI -->|No| SINGLE["Use Direct PR Branch<br>WO Target: Satellite Repo"]
+```
+
+### 2.1 The Slice Branch Invariant
+* **Bridge v2 Single-Target Routing Rule:** A target satellite's CI and downstream consumers must only see diffs relevant to their domain. When multiple targets are touched in a single PR, sharing the broad PR branch would cause satellite diffs (`git diff origin/main...origin/<branch>`) to contain foreign files.
+* **Slice Generation:** For each touched satellite (excluding the master umbrella), `landing.yml` spins up a dedicated branch named `bridge/{task_id}-{slug}` based on `BASE_SHA` and checks out only `tfiles` from `PR_SHA`.
+* **Zero Cross-Talk:** Each satellite receives an atomic, self-contained work order pointing directly to its custom slice branch.
