+## 4. Admin & Superadmin Sovereign Surfaces
+
+Out of the 14 repositories, two anchor the system, while specific satellites enforce strict role boundaries:
+
+### 4.1 Master Monorepo (`Supremeai-bd/supremeai`)
+* **Role Gate:** When non-admin clients (e.g. agents) query the Control Tower for `supremeai`, access is denied:
+  ```text
+  Forbidden: core monorepo 'supremeai' is strictly restricted to admin and supremeadmin roles; 
+  non-admin roles are limited to satellite repos (current role: 'agent').
+  ```
+* **Zero Active Workloads:** Does not run CI runners or cron loops. It serves as a passive mirror that aggregates all satellite commits into one panoramic repository.
+* **Internal Governance:** Retains internal admin decisions (30 active governance records).
+
+### 4.2 Key Vault Gateway (`Supremeai-bd/supremeai-api`)
+* **Ghost Cloaking Moat:** To prevent exposure of LLM API keys and vault secrets, unauthenticated or non-admin callers receive `Repository not found: 'supremeai-api'`.
+* Non-admin agents access the gateway through abstract schema contracts in `supremeai-open/api/`, never reading raw vault configuration.
+
+### 4.3 Sovereign Command Dispatcher (`Supremeai-bd/supremeai-command`)
+* **RBAC Invariant:** Governed strictly by `TELEGRAM_SUPERADMIN_CHAT_ID`. Only the verified Superadmin numeric chat ID can invoke privileged commands (`/stop`, `/pause`, `/voice`, etc.).
